 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Great hobby, there are as many audio shows as there are hours in the day. Some are serious news, some are jokes sent out as jokes but listened to as if they were a secret. Then there are shows about those. The food one is great, you hear chefs practice telling stories with flavor that match what they' talking about. The history one is very entertaining. Not necessarily, but lots of them start out as hobbyist recordings with a simple microphone. You can upgrade later if it turns out to be more than you thought. Then try one episode of a topic you' interested in. If it feels like fun, do more. Most shows leave space at the end for you to say how long you took to get through them.",
